  "description": "Over 60 real names that mean sun or sunshine, from Soleil, Sunniva and Heulwen to Samson, Ravi and Shams, with every meaning checked and sourced.",
  "section": "meanings",
  "published": "2026-11-13",
  "motif": "star",
  "intro": "<p>Sun names come from almost every language: Sol and Soleil from Latin roots, Sunniva and Solveig from Old English and Old Norse, Heulwen from Welsh, Ravi and Surya from Sanskrit, Shams from Arabic, Inti from Quechua. One of the oldest is Samson, from the Hebrew word for sun. Every meaning here has been checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name and Wiktionary, and ranks for England and Wales come from the ONS.</p><p>Some names are sold as sun names on weak evidence. Cyrus, Elio and Eliana are the common ones. We've kept them in, marked uncertain, so you can see what the sources actually say.</p>",
